{"title":"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Sines_and_Cosines)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Sines and Cosines)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Right_Triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Right Triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Bretschneider&#39;s_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Bretschneider's Formula)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Bretschneider&#39;s_Formula\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Bretschneider's Formula</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Symmetry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Symmetry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Note_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MOP_2024\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MOP 2024</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A convex quadrilateral has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62eb33437db419b804749ca1587ecdd77f4ca0c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5, 6, 9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/43420adcd0fce9dce3978d53b97a8e0262b58da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> in that order. Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> the measure of the acute angle formed by the diagonals of the quadrilateral. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/567744e2ef4f7e63710dfcaa23fb8f836c352a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\theta$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Sines_and_Cosines.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Sines_and_Cosines)\">Solution 1 (Sines and Cosines)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Sines and Cosines)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since we are asked to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/567744e2ef4f7e63710dfcaa23fb8f836c352a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\theta$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/865211471c7cc8aff3d88f9f2b843bd262159050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7038458fdc92e1eb1840531bbb58b11dd5ba62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> separately and use their values to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/567744e2ef4f7e63710dfcaa23fb8f836c352a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\theta$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />. We can start by drawing a diagram. Let the vertices of the quadrilateral be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d88d3b225d4dcf1a78380f5c98940f6107e3deca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff67bed50815f029660d4da83fcd8b16c9f9176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed39873efcb4356c2c127a0ae7b7dfc03278a620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 9$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e43ab3616df7169cf742ede9da39ff3dc2ef38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA = 7$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95fea77d5d2c584b40e0b99b2d6ea5851562e180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX = a$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa3dbb031231f10cdc8e6ccad7217ee116509dff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX = b$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f580d6f5bb70a69e41196252ec6f6e2c8850fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX = c$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21d0e37596c156f42cd19fdad62d834c54dd5682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DX = d$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the acute angle formed between the intersection of the diagonals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8fe8bfd35bddd29e1d986195ef4801b7bc8e63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(4cm); pair A,B,C,D,X; A = (0,0); B = (1,0); C = (1.25,-1); D = (-0.75,-0.75); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle,black+1bp); X = intersectionpoint(A--C,B--D); draw(A--C); draw(B--D); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); dot(X); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,S); label(&quot;$5$&quot;,(A+B)/2,N); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,(B+C)/2,E); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(C+D)/2,S); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,(D+A)/2,W); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;,X,2.5E); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,(A+X)/2,NE); label(&quot;$b$&quot;,(B+X)/2,NW); label(&quot;$c$&quot;,(C+X)/2,SW); label(&quot;$d$&quot;,(D+X)/2,SE); [/asy]\" width=\"425\" height=\"232\" />\nWe are given that the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We can express this area using the areas of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/63519827794d69a2ae9aaf52d244205cb79c0235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AXB$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/4296dc042be00297e7a4f47ecaf47cc389b2a6eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BXC$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a8429a1b002e0667108230541ff266241a7fce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CXD$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/3/353f5e2f8d931c58f66d64d28456d381c4e96ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DXA$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />. Since we want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/865211471c7cc8aff3d88f9f2b843bd262159050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7038458fdc92e1eb1840531bbb58b11dd5ba62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />, we can represent these areas using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/865211471c7cc8aff3d88f9f2b843bd262159050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706452485c6b6cec38a2ad349109e199044c6395.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 30 &amp;=[ABCD] \\\\ &amp;=[AXB] + [BXC] + [CXD] + [DXA] \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{2} ab \\sin (\\angle AXB) + \\frac{1}{2} bc \\sin (\\angle BXC) + \\frac{1}{2} cd \\sin (\\angle CXD) + \\frac{1}{2} da \\sin (\\angle AXD) \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{2} ab \\sin (180^\\circ - \\theta) + \\frac{1}{2} bc \\sin (\\theta) + \\frac{1}{2} cd \\sin (180^\\circ - \\theta) + \\frac{1}{2} da \\sin (\\theta). \\end{align*}\" width=\"620\" height=\"130\" />\nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d0688d6f80a25a3a5f20bb0d851940eac3bf460d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (180^\\circ - \\theta) = \\sin \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore it follows that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5633a80c47e07db2b6732c720e79c182aa7933a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 30 &amp;=\\frac{1}{2} ab \\sin (180^\\circ - \\theta) + \\frac{1}{2} bc \\sin (\\theta) + \\frac{1}{2} cd \\sin (180^\\circ - \\theta) + \\frac{1}{2} da \\sin (\\theta) \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{2} ab \\sin (\\theta) + \\frac{1}{2} bc \\sin (\\theta) + \\frac{1}{2} cd \\sin (\\theta) + \\frac{1}{2} da \\sin (\\theta) \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin\\theta (ab + bc + cd + da). \\end{align*}\" width=\"537\" height=\"123\" />\nFrom here we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/3/3f3261fb47bcff8b95c31b5172d06693df3a3b59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta = \\frac{60}{ab + bc + cd + da}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"197\" height=\"39\" />. Now we need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7038458fdc92e1eb1840531bbb58b11dd5ba62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. Using the Law of Cosines on each of the four smaller triangles, we get following equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/aba5dedfa42d6de008fdee28fc64b483ec7b298b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}   5^2 &amp;= a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\\cos(180^\\circ-\\theta), \\\\   6^2 &amp;= b^2 + c^2 - 2bc\\cos \\theta, \\\\   9^2 &amp;= c^2 + d^2 - 2cd\\cos(180^\\circ-\\theta), \\\\   7^2 &amp;= d^2 + a^2 - 2da\\cos \\theta.   \\end{align*}\" width=\"255\" height=\"100\" />\nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897da8c1d5444b5c61aba70555a65bff07c4e935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos (180^\\circ - \\theta) = -\\cos \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"182\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We can substitute this value into our equations to get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421b1dccbb8a99cb753d9cb89c57a85fedb33b36.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}   5^2 &amp;= a^2 + b^2 + 2ab\\cos \\theta, &amp;&amp;(1) \\\\   6^2 &amp;= b^2 + c^2 - 2bc\\cos \\theta, &amp;&amp;(2) \\\\   9^2 &amp;= c^2 + d^2 + 2cd\\cos \\theta, &amp;&amp;(3) \\\\   7^2 &amp;= d^2 + a^2 - 2da\\cos \\theta. &amp;&amp;(4) \\end{align*}\" width=\"301\" height=\"103\" />\nIf we subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7ecdb40a2a6d88500ba2c77294b5039f406ceff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)+(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba9f5a2e009f8b03e34c1f82923169975c8708c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)+(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, the squared terms cancel, leaving us with:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/b/10bcdf694eebcf9410fcfac57cde87173e07d4aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 5^2 + 9^2 - 6^2 - 7^2 &amp;= 2ab \\cos \\theta + 2bc \\cos \\theta + 2cd \\cos \\theta + 2da \\cos \\theta \\\\  21 &amp;= 2\\cos \\theta (ab  + bc + cd + da). \\end{align*}\" width=\"486\" height=\"45\" />\nFrom here we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/9/0890a440eb07a592f3ff733de90199a553d9f7af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta = \\frac{21/2}{ab + bc + cd + da}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"199\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Since we have figured out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/865211471c7cc8aff3d88f9f2b843bd262159050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7038458fdc92e1eb1840531bbb58b11dd5ba62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />, we can calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/567744e2ef4f7e63710dfcaa23fb8f836c352a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\theta$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509d3858cb3bed38db134b26f63a7d0fea216fe6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{\\cos \\theta} = \\frac{\\frac{60}{ab + bc + cd + da}}{\\frac{21/2}{ab + bc + cd + da}} = \\frac{60}{21/2} = \\frac{120}{21} = \\frac{40}{7}.\\]\" width=\"387\" height=\"52\" />\nTherefore our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b4842ceab26e8aef39849b45c3fed6e4f294499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40 + 7 = \\boxed{047}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~ Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p><p>~ my_aops_lessons\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Right_Triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Right_Triangles)\">Solution 2 (Right Triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Right Triangles)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In convex quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/42501e1c7100f340da9bd452bf942219ac6b131b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9f42d1c75b59ea3c2b6d7484813a560a956cae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=5,BC=6,CD=9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"207\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/6/c367dbd44ae30ddf7c18b6f31423fd61eac860be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA=7.$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> be the feet of the perpendiculars from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737b15f20e17e7834a83b8188337bade510f22f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> respectively, to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/3808159e7fa55b110626d243e2734ee0316eb0ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}.$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> We obtain the following diagram:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaad14a17c0f6c7a078d77fa4c6788e26b9409ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(500);  pair A, B, C, D, P, A1, C1; B = origin; D = (3*sqrt(32498*(29400*sqrt(47)+312523))/32498,0); A = intersectionpoints(Circle(B,5),Circle(D,7))[0]; C = intersectionpoints(Circle(B,6),Circle(D,9))[1]; P = intersectionpoint(A--C,B--D); A1 = foot(A,B,D); C1 = foot(C,B,D); markscalefactor=3/160; draw(rightanglemark(A,A1,D),red); draw(rightanglemark(C,C1,B),red); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,1.5*dir(aCos(7/sqrt(1649)))); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,1.5*W); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,1.5*dir(180+aCos(7/sqrt(1649)))); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,1.5*E); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,P,dir(180-(180-aCos(7/sqrt(1649)))/2)); dot(&quot;$A&#39;$&quot;,A1,dir(-75)); dot(&quot;$C&#39;$&quot;,C1,N); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;,P,dir(180+aCos(7/sqrt(1649))/2),red); draw(A--A1^^C--C1,dashed); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle^^A--C^^B--D); [/asy]\" width=\"835\" height=\"378\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b30ae24f165cd0b3bcc845334f2a29a6cac14f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC&#39;=p,C&#39;E=q,EA&#39;=r,A&#39;D=s,AA&#39;=h_1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23cb33672a62594342b3fda32c9a1d8b0d145819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC&#39;=h_2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> We apply the Pythagorean Theorem to right triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/7/2f76869956875494e98207a477b584b4a9a695b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABA&#39;,\\triangle BCC&#39;,\\triangle CDC&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"212\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/0/ac0dadf351dfe4f3f1f6eb5534723be2ef2f70f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DAA&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"19\" /> respectively:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d892a581db85152efa92115ea6c35bd32724782.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{ccccccccccccccccc} (p+q+r)^2&amp;+&amp;h_1^2&amp;=&amp;5^2, &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\\hspace{36mm}(1) \\\\ [1ex] p^2&amp;+&amp;h_2^2&amp;=&amp;6^2, &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\\hspace{36mm}(2) \\\\ [1ex] (q+r+s)^2&amp;+&amp;h_2^2&amp;=&amp;9^2, &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\\hspace{36mm}(3) \\\\ [1ex] s^2&amp;+&amp;h_1^2&amp;=&amp;7^2. &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\\hspace{36mm}(4) \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"616\" height=\"100\" />\nLet the brackets denote areas. We get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcdc2189cf8d7c3f2c93ec59190361210f7a14d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} [ABD]+[CBD]&amp;=[ABCD] \\\\ \\frac12(p+q+r+s)h_1+\\frac12(p+q+r+s)h_2&amp;=30 \\\\ \\frac12(p+q+r+s)(h_1+h_2)&amp;=30 \\\\ (p+q+r+s)(h_1+h_2)&amp;=60. \\hspace{49.25mm}(5) \\end{align*}\" width=\"615\" height=\"131\" />\nWe subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7ecdb40a2a6d88500ba2c77294b5039f406ceff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)+(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b29b586c3ef58ae78d54954689514aa9efa151d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)+(3):$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f3edc91bb17b51407e22eded41aa32c7ade23f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (p+q+r)^2+(q+r+s)^2-p^2-s^2&amp;=21 \\\\ \\left[(p+q+r)^2-s^2\\right]+\\left[(q+r+s)^2-p^2\\right]&amp;=21 \\\\ (p+q+r+s)(p+q+r-s)+(p+q+r+s)(-p+q+r+s)&amp;=21 \\\\ (p+q+r+s)(2q+2r)&amp;=21 \\\\ 2(p+q+r+s)(q+r)&amp;=21 \\\\ (p+q+r+s)(q+r)&amp;=\\frac{21}{2}. \\hspace{9.5mm}(6) \\end{align*}\" width=\"616\" height=\"168\" />\nFrom right triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/c/fcc09394eac7c731530d9804ca7a8f53a4a7b768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEA&#39;$\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8dd7301d5cf5572227bdf502c41d0e2a11a63429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CEC&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc99f9c210b80f529f33539103caad95d307a1cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\theta=\\frac{h_1}{r}=\\frac{h_2}{q}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"134\" height=\"41\" /> It follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/d/7ddfcf2d27c2196dadc03eb8889fe2878bb99e3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{8} \\tan\\theta&amp;=\\frac{h_1}{r}\\qquad&amp;\\implies\\qquad h_1&amp;=r\\tan\\theta, \\hspace{64mm}&amp;(1\\star)\\\\ \\tan\\theta&amp;=\\frac{h_2}{q}\\qquad&amp;\\implies\\qquad h_2&amp;=q\\tan\\theta. &amp;(2\\star) \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"625\" height=\"85\" />\nFinally, we divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737a366a904e00f936f8728869ad8f2587dab46f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/0/520a4d3a2533d8e481041d3c24ee47b2014782c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6):$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/1/1c1f956799cf180059b366db31f832e140d84ed6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{h_1+h_2}{q+r}&amp;=\\frac{40}{7} \\\\ \\frac{r\\tan\\theta+q\\tan\\theta}{q+r}&amp;=\\frac{40}{7} \\hspace{15mm} &amp;&amp;\\text{by }(1\\star)\\text{ and }(2\\star)\\\\ \\frac{(r+q)\\tan\\theta}{q+r}&amp;=\\frac{40}{7} \\\\ \\tan\\theta&amp;=\\frac{40}{7}, \\end{align*}\" width=\"402\" height=\"180\" />\nfrom which the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0b494d8fe5041fa4215eed4d46583bd379899f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40+7=\\boxed{047}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Bretschneider.27s_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Bretschneider's_Formula)\">Solution 3 (Bretschneider's Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Bretschneider&#39;s Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"Bretschneider.27s_Formula\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Bretschneider's_Formula\">Bretschneider's Formula</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Bretschneider&#39;s Formula\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/230b3c79642cd579ca59e6d44347e92acedc4b0a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); import olympiad; defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)+fontsize(10));  pair A,B,C,D; A=origin; B=(1.25,0); D=dir(65); C=D+0.85*dir(90)*(A-D);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(A--C^^B--D, gray+0.5); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NW); label(&quot;$a$&quot;, A--B, S); label(&quot;$b$&quot;, B--C, E); label(&quot;$c$&quot;, D--C, N); label(&quot;$d$&quot;,D--A,W); label(&quot;$u$&quot;,D--B,2*dir(170)); label(&quot;$v$&quot;,A--C,S);  [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"252\" />\nGiven quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, let, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c06de735d79f0b28c30bcbbcf96e67bb1ca42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, be the sides, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> the semiperimeter, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/7/7278fc3f9ba8967a3a367ff2e12c6db9387d1094.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u, v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />, the diagonals. Then the area, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />, is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b517ae14e5ca4fae5986994d53fe34794d3df0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[K = \\tfrac 14 \\sqrt {4u^2v^2-(b^2+d^2-a^2-c^2)^2}\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"32\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>By Bretschneider's Formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef3e879474c6f5ec87e1da1370b9a3a7ded5e6a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[30=\\tfrac{1}{4}\\sqrt{4u^2v^2-(b^2+d^2-a^2-c^2)^2}=\\tfrac{1}{4}\\sqrt{4u^2v^2-441}.\\]\" width=\"436\" height=\"32\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/6/33677ddf538d26dabe59df205f4c85802c07b410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$uv=\\tfrac{3\\sqrt{1649}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"94\" height=\"26\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e164f18f5185f17bb5a77338cd3459c6ad532f0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABCD]=\\tfrac 12 \\cdot uv\\sin{\\theta};\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"21\" /> solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b144c5e51935c5f3229f9dced73af7a45486041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5801cddcd166380e8b5cfe3fa47b0236e64b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\theta}=\\tfrac{40}{\\sqrt{1649}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"102\" height=\"25\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is acute, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c72d3f209ec3895bcf546050ea1526fbb1aaf661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\theta}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> is positive, from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/5/fa5364bac95dabc838bbc6d5ef3ccf83e3043f0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\theta}=\\tfrac{7}{\\sqrt{1649}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4ab2f9357f67da1f9352644730edfed7e23471b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/939f085f096c0cb56f3f9b8c033bf72dedf0f244.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan{\\theta}=\\frac{\\sin{\\theta}}{\\cos{\\theta}}=\\frac{40}{7},\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"37\" /> for a final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef4cb6ff5cda87394f4de3e6643de5c61f3716ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{047}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. \n</p><p>~ Leo.Euler\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Symmetry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Symmetry)\">Solution 4 (Symmetry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Symmetry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AIME-I-2021-12.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/fe/AIME-I-2021-12.png/350px-AIME-I-2021-12.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"350\" height=\"344\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/fe/AIME-I-2021-12.png/525px-AIME-I-2021-12.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/fe/AIME-I-2021-12.png/700px-AIME-I-2021-12.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><i><b>Claim</b></i>\n</p><p>Given an inscribed quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1432c575337862e1370d2419e3c0ae8576f2c07e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = a, BC = b, CD = c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/98716d886078d02dce3801a41b11b224e6ac03aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA = d.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> Prove that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/7/ec7fe6244e09cde63f00c9b42259a8ca60e2c90e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle \\theta &lt; 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> between the diagonals is given by\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf13b1ef2baf29bd0feb015e9c9dc41611ee3994.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}2(ac + bd) \\cos \\theta =  {|d^2 – c^2 + b^2 – a^2|}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"263\" height=\"20\" />\n<i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Let the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be symmetric to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to the perpendicular bisector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a0b75202202b36c2a62a22bba07fc06501bea7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> Then the quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/7/07734da11b9335122d25ca40de278d787e9437ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&#39;CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> is an inscribed one, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7d91ffe5810fe610b406b3281de6ad08a9fb2b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&#39; = b, B&#39;C = a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26e33629af18990899f2f1dad93ca667eaab9cf4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\angle AEB = \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {AB}  + \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {CD}.\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"22\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e446b1e8bdf3df3b0610bff27e13e40b35020115.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2\\angle B&#39;AD = \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {B&#39;C} + \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {CD} = \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {AB} + \\overset{\\Large\\frown} {CD} \\implies \\angle AEB = \\angle B&#39;AD.\\end{align*}\" width=\"479\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>We apply the Law of Cosines to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f8a8e89cb84efb2aeae7366e000bc98993c66c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AB&#39;D$\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/979870b3328ad843c5a227f5a8eef99cd01f7b10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CB&#39;D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"19\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/1/6419c1fa3cd6974751a4b939deb988f2c74705a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} B&#39;D^2 = AD^2 + AB&#39;^2 – 2 AD \\cdot AB&#39; \\cos \\theta, \\end{align*}\" width=\"301\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae3da2662aac48da51820a6c9935897c7477139.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} B&#39;D^2 = CD^2 + CB&#39;^2 + 2 CD \\cdot CB&#39; \\cos \\theta,\\end{align*}\" width=\"317\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/5/d05151dc37b4c018c6abcb6ba4283657912f4128.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} d^2 + b^2 – 2 bd \\cos \\theta = c^2 + a^2 + 2ac \\cos \\theta,\\end{align*}\" width=\"300\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de55bf6de66d559b110c076e8d43e9d7277248ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2(ac + bd) \\cos \\theta = |d^2 – c^2 + b^2 – a^2|.\\end{align*}\" width=\"263\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note_1\">Note 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Note 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By generalization, the tangent of the acute angle formed by the diagonals is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02ef12793809f43878d1f591229157688ad6001e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left|\\frac{4A}{a^2-b^2+c^2-d^2}\\right|.\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MOP_2024\">Video Solution by MOP 2024</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MOP 2024\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/K0u0ACMTSw8\">https://youtu.be/K0u0ACMTSw8</a>\n</p><p>~r00tsOfUnity\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7DxIdTLNbo0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7DxIdTLNbo0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/8GRO4za5rPI\">https://youtu.be/8GRO4za5rPI</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II\" title=\"2021 AIME II\">2021 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2021\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutio